    "notes": "1. Total revenue is mapped directly from 'Revenue'.\n2. Total operating cost is the sum of 'Cost of sales', 'Marketing and selling expenses', 'General and administrative expenses', and 'Other operating income and expenses'. 'Other operating income and expenses' is included as it contains non-recurring operational items like restructuring costs and impairments. 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is excluded as it is an equity-accounted result, not a direct operating cost.\n3. Net income is mapped to 'Net profit, Group share'.\n4. Taxes are mapped directly from 'Income taxes'.\n5. Interest expenses are mapped from 'Cost of net financial debt' and 'Interest on lease liabilities'. 'Other financial income and expenses' is excluded as it contains non-interest items like dividends, FX derivatives, and fair value adjustments.\n6. All values are in EUR millions (scale 1E6). Parentheses in the source indicate negative values; for fields where the sign convention is opposite (costs, taxes, interest), the extracted numbers are positive as they reduce income.\n7. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns but are not used for the core consolidated income statement mapping.",
